---
title: On your site
summary: What Vesper adds to the site it builds, and why all of it is plain static files.
---

Vesper does more than edit content. Every `astro build` also indexes your site for search, checks each built page's accessibility structure, leaves out entries that are scheduled but not yet due, and turns the studio's redirects into pages any host can serve.

Everything it adds is static files in `dist/`, beside the pages Astro builds: the studio at `/admin`, the search index, and a redirect page at each old address. Nothing needs a server, a function or a host setting, so the site works the same on Netlify as on a shared host you upload to by FTP.

The accessibility report is the one thing that stays out of `dist/`. It's written to `.vesper/` in your project, so it's never deployed.
